<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Tarred_Surgery.xml                UtinniPatches — SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1

  "A weak solvent removes it" (item spec, verify section). Shape copied
  from this repo's own RSW_RemoveBrainWorm (src/RimStarWars/BrainWorms/
  Defs/RecipeDefs/Recipes_BrainWormSurgery.xml) — Recipe_RemoveHediff
  (RimWorld/Recipe_RemoveHediff.cs, read in full this pass) is the real
  vanilla worker for "a bill that consumes an ingredient and removes a
  named hediff by def," so no new C# is owed for the cure itself, only for
  making the hediff's own severity track carried filth (this item's piece
  2, RM_HediffComp_CarriedFilthExposure).

  Unlike RSW_RemoveBrainWorm this is NOT risky surgery — no
  deathOnFailedSurgeryChance is set (Anesthetize's own vanilla precedent,
  Data/Core/Defs/RecipeDefs/Recipes_Surgery_Misc.xml, leaves it unset too
  for a routine, non-invasive bill), no skillRequirements (anyone can scrub
  a colonist down), and surgerySuccessChanceFactor is left at the
  SurgeryFlesh abstract default rather than lowered — this is application,
  not incision. isViolation false: applying solvent is not an act of
  violence regardless of who consents.

  ingredients accepts EITHER solvent (RUT_WeakTarSolvent or the foreign-
  trade RUT_StrongTarSolvent, RUT_Tarred_Solvents.xml) via an explicit
  thingDefs filter rather than a shared thingCategory — these two are not a
  general "Medicine"-style pool, they are specifically the two solvents
  this item's own spec names, and nothing else should ever satisfy this
  bill by accident.

  targetsBodyPart false, hideBodyPartNames true — RUT_Tarred carries no
  <part>, matching RSW_RemoveBrainWorm's own choice for a whole-body
  hediff.
-->
<Defs>

  <RecipeDef ParentName="SurgeryFlesh">
    <defName>RUT_ScrubTarred</defName>
    <label>scrub off tar</label>
    <description>Work a solvent into a tarred colonist's skin and hair until the tar lets go. Not surgery in any real sense — just the only thing that gets it off short of waiting it out.</description>
    <workerClass>Recipe_RemoveHediff</workerClass>
    <jobString>Scrubbing off tar.</jobString>
    <workAmount>600</workAmount>
    <hideBodyPartNames>true</hideBodyPartNames>
    <isViolation>false</isViolation>
    <targetsBodyPart>false</targetsBodyPart>
    <removesHediff>RUT_Tarred</removesHediff>
    <successfullyRemovedHediffMessage>{0} has scrubbed the tar off {1}.</successfullyRemovedHediffMessage>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>RUT_WeakTarSolvent</li>
            <li>RUT_StrongTarSolvent</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>2</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>RUT_WeakTarSolvent</li>
        <li>RUT_StrongTarSolvent</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
